A shortcut, not Palm's app.

Palm's Bluetooth app talks to webOS's own Bluetooth service and pairs devices with the
device's radio. Lunacy doesn't own the radio - Android does, so a copy of that UI here could
only pretend. This app is an icon that opens Android's Bluetooth settings instead
(appinfo.json's lunacyAndroidSettings, a Lunacy extension), and it holds no code of its own.
Its id and title are the reference TouchPad's (webOS CE 3.1.0).

icon.png and icon-256x256.png are Palm's, from com.palm.app.bluetoothtab on the reference
TouchPad, so the icon looks like the one webOS users know. Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-
Packard; never released under an open licence; distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like
Mojo and the Prelude fonts.
